hell.command\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49m can select another i\u001b[0m\u001b[13;1H\u001b[0;39;49mnstalled shell.                                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b[14;1H\u001b[0;93;49m-\u001b[0;39;49m A UTF-8 terminal emulator with ANSI/VT control-sequence and SGR mouse-reporting support.\u001b[0m\u001b[15;1H\u001b[0;39;49m Mouse hover and clicks on displayed keys use SGR mouse reporting, which works through ter\u001b[0m\u001b[16;1H\u001b[0;39;49mminal emulators running under X11 or Wayland.                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[17;1H\u001b[0;93;49m-\u001b[0;39;49m On the Linux virtual console, an active GPM daemon can provide mouse hover and click inp\u001b[0m\u001b[18;1H\u001b[0;39;49mut. GPM support is optional; no extra Go dependency is required.                          \u001b[0m\u001b[19;1H\u001b[0;93;49m-\u001b[0;39;49m An 80-column by 24-row terminal is recommended. Smaller windows may cause the keyboard l\u001b[0m\u001b[20;1H\u001b[0;39;49mayout to wrap or overlap.                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b[21;1H\u001b[0;39;49m                                                                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[22;1H\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m## \u001b[0;38;5;225;49mDependencies\u001b[0;39;49m                                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b[23;1H\u001b[0;39;49m                                                                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[24;1H\u001b[0;39;49mGo modules are downloaded automatically by the Go toolchain. Direct module dependencies ar\u001b[0m\u001b[25;1H\u001b[0;39;49me:                                                                                        \u001b[0m\u001b[26;1H\u001b[0;39;49m                                                                                          \u001b[0m\u001b[27;1H\u001b[0;93;49m-\u001b[0;39;49m [\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49mgithub.com/creack/pty\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49m](\u001b[0;95;49mhttps://github.com/creack/pty\u001b[0;39;49m): starts and resizes the shell p\u001b[0m\u001b[28;1H\u001b[0;39;49mseudo-terminal.                                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b[29;1H\u001b[0;93;49m-\u001b[0;39;49m [\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49mgithub.com/hinshun/vt10x\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49m](\u001b[0;95;49mhttps://github.com/hinshun/vt10x\u001b[0;39;49m): emulates the shell's VT \u001b[0m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[0;39;49mscreen and control sequences.                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b[31;1H\u001b[0;93;49m-\u001b[0;39;49m [\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49mgolang.org/x/term\u001b[0;38;5;224;49m`\u001b[0;39;49m](\u001b[0;95;49mhttps://pkg.go.dev/golang.org/x/t"]
